    "created_at": "2026-10-01T18:23:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T18:23:57Z",
    "body": "Current Chromium looks like it may have moved since this was filed. `USBDevice::OnConnectionError()` now rejects every pending `device_requests_` resolver with `NotFoundError` and `\"The device was disconnected.\"`, including an outstanding `transferIn()`.\n\nThat seems to implement the first suggestion here already. A focused WPT that starts a pending `transferIn()`, disconnects the fake device, and asserts `NotFoundError` would tell us whether this can now be closed or whether there is still a platform-specific ordering problem.\n",
